    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίζ-ωμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the mass of roots</i> of a tree, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>element</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέσσαρα μὲν πάντων ῥιζώματα πρῶτον
					ἄκουε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					6.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀενάου φύσεως ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
				15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>stem, race</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				413
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείων δ᾽ ἀπ᾽ ἀμφοῖν ἔκγονον
				ῥιζωμάτων</span>, i.e. on the side of both parents, <i><span class="en">
				Theodect.
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
